			<td align="Center"><font color="White">
										<P>Title:&nbsp;
											<span id="dl_news__ctl0_Label4"><font color="White">First Brood Harvest </font></span></P>
										<P>Date:
											<span id="dl_news__ctl0_Label2"><font color="White">Nov 19 2002  8:34PM</font></span></P>
										<P>
											<span id="dl_news__ctl0_Label1"><font color="White">Its that time of the year again....<BR>The weather is changing. Its getting colder and leaves are falling off trees from all the druids humping them. And the best part being First Broods Ripe for the pickin` !<BR><BR><IMG src="http://home.mchsi.com/~serendipitousexistence/clown.jpg"><BR><BR>First we discovered a Klandicar just ready to plucked from the fertile DN Valley. He was harvested with little effort and since we hate him so much, Kortan walked away with a new sleepers key.<BR><BR>But this wasn`t going to be the only harvest of the eve, oh no.... We heard rumors of these Deep Cavern First Broods. So into DN we plunged, cutting through armies of rats to find this most precious bounty. And then there it was...<BR><BR><IMG src="http://home.mchsi.com/~serendipitousexistence/zlan.jpg"><BR><BR>Zlandicar lay before us maybe a little too ripe as we soon discovered....but this didn`t stop us from harvesting him, for as any First Brood Harvester knows, the truly good part of a First Brood comes from the pit being it`s talisman. Gratz Angyll on this sleepers key, and Stephania on the Frak Talisman for a Shroud of the Dar Brood. His vile still beating heart went to the guild bank for bubble gum money.<BR><BR>I r roleplayer.<BR><BR>oh ya we got owned by RoS later just for fun.........<BR><BR>sani<BR></font></span></P>
